          "text": "You are an expert TikTok Live coach. Generate a structured 4-phase outline a creator can glance at during their live. This is a cheat sheet, not a full script. Keep it short, scannable, and actionable.\n\n---\n\nCREATOR PROFILE:\nName: {{ $json.creatorName }}\nGender: {{ $json.gender }}\nBio: {{ $json.bio }}\nTagline: {{ $json.tagline }}\nMy Goal: {{ $json.myGoal }}\nLooking For: {{ $json.lookingFor }}\nGeneration: {{ $json.generation }}\nRegional Accent: {{ $json.regionalAccent }}\nAudience Size: {{ $json.audienceSize }}\n\n---\n\nLIVE DETAILS:\nLive Type: {{ $json.liveType }}\nTopic / Theme: {{ $json.topic }}\nCreator Notes: {{ $json.notes }}\n\n---\n\nGIFT GOAL GUIDANCE:\nSet a realistic gift goal based on the creator's audience size. Use these benchmarks:\n- Under 1K followers: 10-20 Roses (low commitment, builds habit)\n- 1K-5K followers: 30-50 Roses\n- 5K-10K followers: 50-100 Roses or 5-10 GG\n- 10K-50K followers: 100-300 Roses or 10-30 GG\n- 50K+ followers: Scale based on typical live engagement\n\nIf audience size is not available, suggest a modest starting goal and tell the creator to adjust up or down based on their experience.\n\nThe gift goal should feel collaborative ('let's hit this together') not desperate. Give a specific goal announcement script they can say word-for-word.\n\n---\n\n4-PHASE FRAMEWORK:\n\nPhase 1 - Opening:\n- Welcome script: a suggested opening line that sounds like this creator (use their bio and tagline for voice)\n- Promise: what to tell viewers they are getting from this live — give a reason to stay\n- Engagement hook: an opening question or prompt to get comments flowing early\n\nPhase 2 - Value Delivery:\n- 3-5 talking points based on the topic/theme\n- 2-3 engagement prompts (questions to ask during this phase)\n- Transition line: a natural sentence to move from value into the monetisation phase without it feeling forced\n\nPhase 3 - Monetisation Integration:\n- Gift goal moment: when and how to announce the LIVE Goal\n- 2-3 gifting moment triggers: natural points to encourage gifts (after delivering value, during progress checks, during milestone celebrations)\n- Acknowledgment reminders: small gift = brief thanks by name, medium = pause and celebrate, large = stop everything and make a moment\n- Progress check script: a line for updating viewers on goal progress\n\nPhase 4 - Closing:\n- Wrap-up warning script: signal you are wrapping up to create last-minute urgency\n- Recap points: what was covered\n- Thank you script: thank top supporters by name\n- Next live tease: when you will be back and give a reason to return\n\nSHOPPABLE LIVE ADDITIONS (only if Live Type is Shoppable):\n- Product talking points: key selling points to weave into Phase 2\n- Demo moment: when to demonstrate the product during the live\n- 2-3 purchase prompt scripts: word-for-word lines for directing viewers to the shop link or basket\n\nIf Live Type is Regular, do not include the shoppable additions.\n\n---\n\nVOICE RULES:\n- The welcome script, goal announcement, transition line, progress check, wrap-up warning, thank you, and next live tease should sound like this creator. Use their bio and tagline to match their natural voice.\n- Everything else (talking points, engagement prompts, structural guidance) should be clear and neutral.\n- Keep the whole outline scannable. Short bullet points. No paragraphs.\n- This is a cheat sheet they look at while live, not something they read out. The scripts are the only word-for-word parts.\n\n---\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON. No text before or after.\n\n{\n  \"concept_name\": \"[Short descriptive name for this live outline — max 5 words]\",\n  \"full_script\": \"[The complete 4-phase outline in markdown format. Use ## for phase headers, **bold** for sub-sections, - for bullet points. Include all scripts, talking points, engagement prompts, gift goal, and shoppable additions if applicable. This is the entire outline in one string.]\"\n}\n\nCRITICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n- Return ONLY valid JSON with no text before or after\n- full_script must be a single string containing the full outline in markdown\n- Include the gift goal with a specific number and a word-for-word announcement script\n- Shoppable additions only appear when Live Type is Shoppable\n- Scripts should sound like this specific creator, not generic\n- Keep it scannable — bullet points, not paragraphs\n- If creator profile fields are empty, work with what is provided"
